;; expect: main.apart refused pattern_type
;; a row's representation is not an E-first body's to read. A ByteArray runs as Init's List
;; cells, and this body — E-first: it binds a match of a numeral under a constructor — would take
;; it apart with List's
;; constructors; the classifier's pass refuses every constructor pattern on a row's type, as
;; the elaborator does on the typed route (pattern_constructor), so the lowering may give the
;; type another layout behind the same signatures. An `if` on one is if_type
(fn apart ((b ByteArray)) Nat
  (let
    ((k Nat
       (match (List.cons 1 List.nil)
         ((List.cons 1 _) 1)
         (_ 0))))
    (match b
      (List.nil 0)
      ((List.cons h t) h))))
